<title>SWEDEN: Fewer Swedish market players see EMU in 1999 - poll.</title>
<headline>Fewer Swedish market players see EMU in 1999 - poll.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>A March survey by pollster TEMO showed fewer Swedish market players expected Europe's economic and monetary union (EMU) to start as planned in 1999, or 68 percent compared to 80 percent in February.</p>
<p>The poll also showed that seven percent of market players believed Sweden would join EMU from the start, down from 10 percent at the time of a previous poll in February.  </p>
<p>Players expected the spread between five-year Swedish bond yields and German ones to be 45 basis points if both Sweden and Germany were members of EMU, up from 39 points in February.</p>
<p>The poll was commissioned by Ohman brokerage and included responses from 73 players on Sweden's stock and debt markets.</p>
<p>-- Birgitta Forsberg, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
